s 5y 0.32), so read it loosely.","About $94.5M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 40% in the 2020 crash, 25% in the 2022 bear market and 31% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its blended-model fair value of $32.73 (margin of safety -39%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 13%).","On multiples it looks expensive against Utilities peers: EV/EBITDA 15.7 vs 12.5 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 32% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an EBIT/EV of 4.2% (vs the 8% bar).","The 5 covering analysts target $41.20 on average, 9% below the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 6% falls short of the cost of capital of 6.1%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have been steady (CV 0.21).","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.64x.","ROE of 9% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.8x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.5% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 6.1x net debt to EBITDA ($34.8M of cash against $8.2B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 2.8x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.06 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD.","The current ratio of 0.80 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 2.6% over 3 years, 11.1% over 5 years and 11.8% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 18%).","Capex runs 3.4x depreciation (59.2% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and institutions hold 82%.","It returns 2.8% a year to shareholders (3.2% in dividends, less 0.1% of net share issuance).","It has paid a dividend for 39 consecutive years, raising it 10.0% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 3,303 employees, each generates about $749K of revenue, 0.7x the Utilities median, and productivity has risen 8.5% a year.","CEO pay is $3.4M (4x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":25,"head":"Avoid: priced 39% above its fair value of $32.73.","pros":["Revenue grew 11.1%/yr over 5y"],"cons":["Trades 39% above fair value of $32.73","ROIC 5.7% vs WACC 6.1%","Net debt/EBITDA 6.1x","Interest coverage only 2.8x","EV/EBITDA 15.7x vs sector 12.5x"],"flags":["Priced 39% above its fair value of $32.73"],"need":[],"buy_below":27.82,"vc":{"base":32.73,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":32.73,"n_alt":3,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.1308,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":20.4014,"ev_ebitda":12.539,"pfcf":19.6541,"pb":1.8576,"roic":0.0568,"gross_margin":0.3591,"fcf_margin":-0.0633,"div_yield":0.0329}},"ticker":"WTRG","date":"2026-11-06"}